---
import Layout from "../../Base.astro";
import SimpleHero from "../../components/SimpleHero.astro";
import FeaturedArticles from "../../components/FeaturedArticles.astro";
import ServicesRelatedWork from "../../components/ServicesRelatedWork.astro";
import "../../styles/pages/_services-list.scss";
---

<Layout
  title="Motion Graphics &amp; Explainer Animation | Kelp"
  description="Motion graphics that explain products, processes, and data across websites, campaigns, presentations, and social channels."
>
  <SimpleHero
    tagline="Content Creation Services"
    title="Motion Graphics"
    description="When the story is complex, static visuals can only carry so much weight. We use motion graphics to explain, emphasize, and make important ideas easier to remember."
    lottieFile="motion-graphics.json"
  />
  <div class="service-body">
    <div class="wrapper wrapper--narrow">
      <h2>Where teams get stuck</h2>
      <p>
        Some ideas are hard to explain with static visuals alone. Products,
        processes, data, and layered stories often need more pacing and more
        guidance than a still graphic can provide.
      </p>
      <p>
        When attention is limited, motion can help the audience follow the idea
        instead of dropping off halfway through it.
      </p>
      <h2>How we fix it</h2>
      <p>
        We use animation, pacing, typography, sound, and sequencing to make the
        message easier to understand and more memorable once it lands.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Case studies</li>
        <li>Data visualizations</li>
        <li>Product reviews</li>
        <li>Explainer videos</li>
        <li>Testimonials</li>
        <li>Promotion</li>
        <li>Sales collateral</li>
        <li>Social media</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>Start with the Message</h2>
      <p>
        We map the audience, format, script, visual direction, and intended
        action before animation begins. The result may be an explainer, data
        sequence, product demonstration, campaign asset, or set of social
        cutdowns. Pacing and clarity matter more than adding movement for its
        own sake.
      </p>
      <h2>Design for Where It Will Play</h2>
      <p>
        A muted social placement, a website section, and an on-site screen have
        different constraints. We plan versions and captions around those
        contexts. <a href="/work/elev8-fun/">Elev8 Fun</a> shows motion supporting the wider campaign and
        physical experience. Discuss your motion project.
      </p>
      <h2>How This Works in Practice</h2>
      <p>
        Motion can explain a sequence, emphasize a change, or give a campaign a
        recognizable rhythm. We choose it for the message and placement rather
        than adding animation to every asset. Storyboards establish what the
        viewer needs to learn; design and timing help that point land quickly.
        Deliverables can then be adapted for the website, social platforms,
        presentations, or paid placements.
      </p>
      <h2>What the Work Includes</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Explainer and process animation</li>
        <li>Campaign and social motion</li>
        <li>Data visualization and title sequences</li>
        <li>Captioned versions and delivery formats</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>What Moving Forward Looks Like</h2>
      <p>
        Bring the message, intended channel, target length, and any existing
        brand or footage. We can help determine whether animation is the right
        format and what it should explain.
      </p>
      <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
      <h3>Will the video work without sound?</h3>
      <p>
        When it needs to, we plan the visual sequence and captions so the core
        message survives muted playback.
      </p>
      <p>
        <a href="/contact/" class="button button--green">
          Talk Through Your Motion Project
        </a>
      </p>
    </div>
    <ServicesRelatedWork tag={76} />
  </div>
  <FeaturedArticles />
</Layout>
